== District 4 ==
{{see also|Texas's 4th congressional district}}
The 4th district serves an area of [[Northeast Texas]], that includes some counties along the [[Red River of the South|Red River]] northeast of the [[Dallas/Fort Worth Metroplex]]. The incumbent is Republican [[John Ratcliffe (American politician)|John Ratcliffe]], who has served since 2015. He was reelected in 2016 with 87.99%, facing no Democratic opponent. The PVI of the district is R+28, making it one of the most conservative districts in the nation.

