== District 5 ==
{{see also|Texas's 5th congressional district}}
The 5th district serves an area that includes the southeast portion of [[Dallas County, Texas|Dallas County]] including [[Mesquite, Texas|Mesquite]] plus a number of smaller counties south and east of Dallas including [[Anderson County, Texas|Anderson]], [[Cherokee County, Texas|Cherokee]], [[Henderson County, Texas|Henderson]] and [[Kaufman County, Texas|Kaufman]] counties. At the 2000 [[census]], the 5th district  represented 651,620 people. The current Representative from District 5 is [[Jeb Hensarling]], who has served since 2003. He was reelected in 2016 with 80.61% of the vote, facing no Democratic opponent. The PVI of this district is R+16. Hensarling announced in October 2017 that he is going to retire from [[United States Congress|Congress]], and not seek re-election to another term in 2018.<ref>{{cite news |last=Ackerman |first=Andrew |date=October 31, 2017 |title=GOP Rep. Jeb Hensarling of Texas Won’t Seek Re-Election |url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/gop-rep-jeb-hensarling-of-texas-wont-seek-re-election-1509475403 |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |location=New York |access-date=October 31, 2017 }}</ref>

