== District 22 ==
{{see also|Texas's 22nd congressional district}}
The 22nd district covers a largely suburban south-central portion of the {{nowrap|[[Greater Houston]]}} metropolitan area. The district includes the majority of [[Fort Bend County, Texas|Fort Bend County]], including most of the cities of [[Sugar Land, Texas|Sugar Land]], [[Missouri City, Texas|Missouri City]], [[Rosenberg, Texas|Rosenberg]], [[Needville, Texas|Needville]] and the county seat of [[Richmond, Texas|Richmond]] as well as the county's share of the largely unincorporated [[Greater Katy]] area west of Houston. In addition, the district also contains portions of northern [[Brazoria County]] including [[Pearland, Texas|Pearland]] and [[Alvin, Texas|Alvin]] as well as a small portion of southeast Harris County centered on [[Friendswood, Texas|Friendswood]]. The district is currently represented by Republican [[Pete Olson]], serving since 2009. Olson was reelected with 59.52% of the vote in 2016. The district's PVI is R+10.

