== District 32 ==
{{see also|Texas's 32nd congressional district}}
The 32nd district serves a suburban area of northeastern [[Dallas, Texas]]. It is represented by Republican [[Pete Sessions]], serving since 1997. He was reelected with 71.07% of the vote in 2016 without a Democratic opponent. The district's PVI is R+5, due to [[United States presidential election, 2016|2016]] Democratic presidential candidate [[Hillary Clinton]]'s performance in the district. Sessions is running for reelection. Six Democrats are also running, including civil rights attorney and former NFL player [[Colin Allred]], longtime Democratic operative Ed Meier, and former [[Department of Agriculture]] official Lilian Salerno.

