== District 33 ==
{{see also|Texas's 33rd congressional district}}
The 33rd district is composed of two counties in Texas—[[Dallas County, Texas|Dallas County]] and [[Tarrant County, Texas|Tarrant County]]. In Dallas County, the district covers parts of [[Dallas]], [[Irving, Texas|Irving]], and [[Grand Prairie, Texas|Grand Prairie]], and all of [[Cockrell Hill, Texas|Cockrell Hill]]. In Tarrant County, the district includes parts of [[Arlington, Texas|Arlington]], [[Forest Hill, Texas|Forest Hill]], [[Fort Worth, Texas|Fort Worth]], [[Grand Prairie, Texas|Grand Prairie]], [[Haltom City, Texas|Haltom City]], [[Saginaw, Texas|Saginaw]] and [[Sansom Park, Texas|Sansom Park]], and all of [[Everman, Texas|Everman]]. It is currently represented by Democrat [[Marc Veasey]], and has been since the district's creation in 2013. Veasey was reelected with 73.71% of the vote in 2016. The district's PVI is D+23.

