== District 36 ==
{{see also|Texas's 36th congressional district}}
The 36th district is located in [[southeast Texas]] and includes all of [[Newton County, Texas|Newton]], [[Jasper County, Texas|Jasper]], [[Tyler County, Texas|Tyler]], [[Polk County, Texas|Polk]], [[Orange County, Texas|Orange]], [[Hardin County, Texas|Hardin]], [[Liberty County, Texas|Liberty]], and [[Chambers County, Texas|Chambers]] counties, plus portions of southeastern [[Harris County, Texas|Harris County]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://gis1.tlc.state.tx.us/?PlanHeader=PLANc185|title=DistrictViewer - Texas Legislative Council|website=gis1.tlc.state.tx.us|accessdate=May 24, 2018}}</ref>  The [[Johnson Space Center]] is within the district. It is currently represented by Republican [[Brian Babin]], who has served since 2015. Babin was reelected in 2016 with 88.61% of the vote, without a Democratic opponent. Two Democrats have announced their candidacy, scientist/environmental consultant Jon Powell and radio and television personality [[Dayna Steele]].

